[2026-09-26T14:24:12.009+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] Use this skill when you determine the current node owns the smallest executable feature slice required by its scenarios.
[2026-09-26T14:24:12.009+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 
[2026-09-26T14:24:12.009+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] ## Instructions
[2026-09-26T14:24:12.009+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 
[2026-09-26T14:24:12.009+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 1. Treat the current node as owning the smallest executable feature slice required by its scenarios.
[2026-09-26T14:24:12.009+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 2. Design only interfaces needed for the owned chain, which may span UI -> API -> FUNC -> DB when those layers are truly owned by the leaf.
[2026-09-26T14:24:12.009+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 3. Prefer existing entrypoints, boundary files, services, and persistence scaffolds before creating new owners.
[2026-09-26T14:24:12.009+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 4. Reuse existing parent/dependency interfaces when the leaf should implement, extend, or call them; return the existing `interface_id` so the current node can be attached to the same contract.
[2026-09-26T14:24:12.009+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 5. If a parent-designed UI shell is the user-facing entry for the leaf, include that UI interface in the leaf's interface list and connect it to leaf-owned API/FUNC/DB interfaces through callers/callees.
[2026-09-26T14:24:12.009+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 6. Materialize only minimal compilable owner files or skeleton code during DESIGN when the interface would otherwise be only abstract JSON.
[2026-09-26T14:24:12.009+08:00] [InterfaceDesigner][REQ-1-1-1] 7. Do not implement full validation, persistence, authentication/session semantics, encryption, or business behavior in DESIGN; that belongs to TestDrivenDeveloper.
